  "label": "Metaphor of Hide and Seek for Missing Person",
  "description": "The phrase 'my dad is the best at hide and seek' is a metaphorical expression used to describe a parent who is absent or missing. In this context, 'hide and seek' is not a literal game but a symbolic representation of the father's prolonged absence, suggesting he is 'hiding' or 'gone' for an extended period. This metaphor is culturally understood as a way to express the emotional impact of parental loss or disappearance.",
